---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import '../styles/global.css';

const stories = [
  {
    name: 'Sarah T.',
    before: 'C5',
    after: 'A2',
    duration: '3 months',
    subject: 'O-Level English',
    subjectKey: 'english',
    quote: '"I used to dread comprehension passages. Now I actually enjoy pulling them apart — it\'s like solving a puzzle."',
    quoteAttr: '— Sarah T., Sec 4',
    paragraphs: [
      'When Sarah first joined A-Worthy, she struggled most with inference questions and summary writing. Her answers were vague and lacked the precision examiners look for. She would often write what she felt the passage meant rather than what the text actually supported.',
      'With the SHARP Method, Sarah learned to read a comprehension passage the way a lawyer reads a brief: find the key claims, follow the author\'s argument, and back every answer with words from the text. Each week her tutor worked with her on annotating passages, which gave her a way into even the hardest inference questions.',
      'By her third month, Sarah\'s summary scores had gone from 4/8 to a steady 7/8, and her English grade had moved from C5 to A2. The careful reading carried over to her other subjects too.'
    ],
    milestones: [
      { week: 'Week 2', text: 'Started using EIL (Evidence, Implication, Link) for every inference question' },
      { week: 'Week 6', text: 'Summary scores improved from 4/8 to 7/8' },
      { week: 'Week 12', text: 'Scored A2 in her school prelims' }
    ]
  },
  {
    name: 'Marcus L.',
    before: 'D7',
    after: 'B3',
    duration: '4 months',
    subject: 'O-Level English',
    subjectKey: 'english',
    quote: '"My parents couldn\'t believe the change. I went from failing English to actually looking forward to the exam."',
    quoteAttr: '— Marcus L., Sec 4',
    paragraphs: [
      'Marcus came to A-Worthy with a D7 in English and very little confidence. His compositions were disorganised, his vocabulary was limited, and he often ran out of time in exams. His parents were worried English would drag down his whole L1R5 score.',
      'His tutor started with the basics: building sentences, organising paragraphs and managing time. The SHARP Method gave Marcus the same structure to follow in every composition and comprehension paper, so he always had somewhere to start instead of a blank page.',
      'Over four months, his compositions went from rambling stories to tightly structured essays with clear topic sentences and evidence to back them. He read faster once he could spot question types quickly. By the end, Marcus scored a B3, four grades up, and it opened up his JC options.'
    ],
    milestones: [
      { week: 'Week 3', text: 'Planned every composition with a story spine' },
      { week: 'Week 8', text: 'Reading faster and answering comprehension more accurately' },
      { week: 'Week 16', text: 'Went from D7 to B3 in O-Level English' }
    ]
  },
  {
    name: 'Priya K.',
    before: 'C6',
    after: 'A1',
    duration: '5 months',
    subject: 'O-Level English',
    subjectKey: 'english',
    quote: '"The SHARP Method didn\'t just help me in English — it changed how I think about every subject."',
    quoteAttr: '— Priya K., Sec 4',
    paragraphs: [
      'Priya worked hard but couldn\'t get past a C. She understood the content but couldn\'t yet put her ideas across the way A-grade answers do. Her oral scores were pulling her down too.',
      'Her tutor saw that the gap was depth of analysis. She would describe what a passage said but rarely asked why the author made particular choices. The SHARP Method taught her to comment on language, tone and the writer\'s techniques, and she used that in both her written and oral answers.',
      'In month three, Priya scored her first A for a timed essay. After that she started volunteering for oral practice, and her spoken English came on quickly. In the O-Level exam she scored an A1, the top grade.'
    ],
    milestones: [
      { week: 'Week 4', text: 'Learned the vocabulary for commenting on language' },
      { week: 'Week 12', text: 'Scored her first A in a timed essay' },
      { week: 'Week 20', text: 'Scored A1 in O-Level English' }
    ]
  },
  {
    name: 'Wei Jie C.',
    before: 'B4',
    after: 'A2',
    duration: '2 months',
    subject: 'O-Level English',
    subjectKey: 'english',
    quote: '"I was so close to an A but couldn\'t figure out what was missing. A-Worthy showed me exactly what examiners want."',
    quoteAttr: '— Wei Jie C., Sec 4',
    paragraphs: [
      'Wei Jie was already doing reasonably well with a B4, but his family felt he could reach a distinction. His school teachers praised his effort but couldn\'t pin down why his answers kept falling just short of an A.',
      'His A-Worthy tutor found the gap quickly. Wei Jie\'s answers were accurate but didn\'t evaluate: he said what the text said, not how or why it worked. Two changes made the difference straight away: adding evaluation to his comprehension answers, and writing stronger essay conclusions.',
      'Within two months, Wei Jie was scoring A grades. His comprehension scores rose by 8 marks on average, and his compositions gained the analysis they had been missing. He scored an A2 in the O-Level exam. The gap had been technique, not effort.'
    ],
    milestones: [
      { week: 'Week 1', text: 'Assessment showed the gap: answers that didn\'t evaluate' },
      { week: 'Week 4', text: 'Comprehension scores improved by 8 marks on average' },
      { week: 'Week 8', text: 'Reached A2, a distinction' }
    ]
  },
  {
    name: 'Aisha M.',
    before: 'U',
    after: 'B',
    duration: '6 months',
    subject: 'H1 General Paper',
    subjectKey: 'gp',
    quote: '"GP felt like a guessing game until A-Worthy. The frameworks made every question answerable — I always knew where to start."',
    quoteAttr: '— Aisha M., JC 2',
    paragraphs: [
      'Aisha came to A-Worthy at the end of JC 1 with a U for her GP promotional exam. She read widely, followed the news and could talk sensibly about almost any issue. On paper, though, her essays wandered, her counter-arguments were thin, and her application question (AQ) answers missed the mark every time.',
      'Her tutor spotted the problem in one lesson: Aisha was thinking in points, not arguments. The SHARP Method gave her a system. The P-E-E-L framework (Point, Evidence, Explanation, Link) turned scattered ideas into structured paragraphs, and the Evaluation Matrix made her weigh counter-arguments before she wrote a word. The AQ Response Template gave her an opening she could use every time without losing marks.',
      'Over six months, Aisha rebuilt her GP from the ground up. She kept a bank of arguments sorted by theme, wrote one timed essay every week, and learned to mark her own work against the official Cambridge band descriptors. She was at a B by the prelims and held it at the A-Levels, five grades up.'
    ],
    milestones: [
      { week: 'Week 2', text: 'Started writing paragraphs with P-E-E-L' },
      { week: 'Week 12', text: 'AQ scores reached Band 3' },
      { week: 'Week 24', text: 'Scored B in H1 General Paper at A-Level' }
    ]
  },
  {
    name: 'Daniel O.',
    before: 'U',
    after: 'A',
    duration: '8 months',
    subject: 'H2 Economics',
    subjectKey: 'econ',
    quote: '"I went from blank-staring at case studies to actually enjoying them. The DEED structure changed everything for me."',
    quoteAttr: '— Daniel O., JC 2',
    paragraphs: [
      'Daniel scored a U for H2 Economics in his JC 1 promotional exam. He knew the theory and could recite definitions and draw diagrams from memory, but his essays read like a textbook and his case study answers ignored the data completely. He was close to dropping the subject.',
      'His A-Worthy tutor worked on applying what he knew, not on more content. The DEED framework (Define, Explain, Evaluate, Diagram) gave Daniel a clear structure for every essay paragraph. The Extract-Link-Apply technique made him use the case study data instead of writing around it, and quick diagram drills at the start of every lesson turned his shaky AD-AS curves into accurate, fully labelled diagrams.',
      'Eight months later, Daniel scored an A in H2 Economics at A-Level. The following year he applied to read Economics at NUS, something he would have ruled out the year before.'
    ],
    milestones: [
      { week: 'Week 3', text: 'Wrote his first essay using the DEED structure' },
      { week: 'Week 16', text: 'Case study answers scoring in the L3 band' },
      { week: 'Week 32', text: 'Scored A in H2 Economics at A-Level' }
    ]
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title="Success Stories | Six A-Worthy Students, Before and After" description="Six A-Worthy students in O-Level English, H1 GP and H2 Economics: where each one started, what changed in lessons, and the grade they finished with.">
  <Header slot="header" />

  <!-- ===== HERO ===== -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-content">
      <span class="eyebrow">Success Stories</span>
      <h1>How six students&rsquo; <span class="accent-word">grades</span> changed</h1>
      <p class="hero-subtitle">Four in O-Level English, one in H1 General Paper and one in H2 Economics. Each story shows where the student started, what changed with the SHARP Method (See, Hit, Apply, Refine, Practise) and the grade they finished with.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions" data-track="hero">
        <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn-accent">Book Free Assessment</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <img src="/images/mascots/mascot-family.webp" alt="" width="480" height="477" class="sticker sticker--hero" />
  </section>

  <!-- ===== STORIES ===== -->
  <section class="section stories-section">
    <div class="container">
      {stories.map((story, i) => (
        <article class="story-card card-lift">
          <div class="story-header">
            <div class="story-grade-change">
              <span class="grade grade-before chip chip--pink">{story.before}</span>
              <span class="grade-arrow"><span class="sr-only">to</span>
                <svg aria-hidden="true" width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-accent)" stroke-width="2"><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/><polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19"/></svg>
              </span>
              <span class="grade grade-after chip chip--green">{story.after}</span>
            </div>
            <div class="story-meta">
              <h2 class="story-name">{story.name}</h2>
              <span class="story-subject">{story.subject}</span>
              <span class="story-duration-badge chip">{story.duration}</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="story-body">
            {story.paragraphs.map((p: string) => (
              <p>{p.split('A-Worthy').map((part: string, i: number) => i === 0 ? part : [<span class="nobr">A-Worthy</span>, part])}</p>
            ))}
          </div>

          <div class="story-timeline">
            <h3 class="timeline-heading">Key milestones</h3>
            <div class="timeline">
              {story.milestones.map((m: { week: string; text: string }) => (
                <div class="timeline-item">
                  <span class="timeline-marker"></span>
                  <div class="timeline-content">
                    <span class="timeline-week">{m.week}</span>
                    <span class="timeline-text">{m.text}</span>
                  </div>
                </div>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>

          <blockquote class="story-quote">
            <p>{story.quote}</p>
            <cite>{story.quoteAttr}</cite>
          </blockquote>

          <div class="story-cta" data-track="story">
            <a href={`/contact/?subject=${story.subjectKey}`} class="btn btn-accent">Book Free Assessment</a>
          </div>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===== CTA ===== -->
  <section class="section cta-section" data-track="final-cta">
    <div class="container" style="text-align: center; max-width: 40rem;">
      <span class="eyebrow">Your Turn</span>
      <h2 class="section-heading text-center">Start with your child&rsquo;s latest test or exam</h2>
      <p class="cta-desc">Send us a photo of the paper, and Jeremy will send you a free written report on the gaps and the programme we recommend.</p>
      <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn-accent">Book Free Assessment</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Uses the sticker-book tokens + vocabulary from global.css. */

  /* ===== HERO ===== */
  .hero {
    padding: 1.25rem 0 1rem;
    text-align: center;
    background: var(--bg-secondary);
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .hero-content {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 var(--page-padding);
  }
  .hero h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    font-weight: 900;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.15;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .hero-subtitle {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.7;
    max-width: 500px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .hero-actions {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  /* ===== STORY CARDS — white ink stickers that lift on hover ===== */
  .story-card {
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 2px solid var(--color-ink);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    box-shadow: 0 3px 0 var(--ink-shadow);
    padding: 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    transition: transform 0.22s cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1), box-shadow 0.22s ease;
  }
  @media (hover: hover) {
    .story-card:hover {
      transform: translateY(-2px);
      box-shadow: 0 6px 0 var(--ink-shadow), 0 12px 24px rgba(70, 50, 20, 0.10);
    }
  }
  .story-card:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .story-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    padding-bottom: 1rem;
    border-bottom: 2px dashed var(--ink-faint);
  }

  .story-grade-change {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  /* Before / after grades are .chip--pink / .chip--green; only the size is page-specific */
  .grade.chip {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    padding: 0.4rem 1rem;
    min-height: 44px;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }
  .grade-arrow {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .story-meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.25rem;
  }
  .story-name {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .story-subject {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .story-duration-badge {
    width: fit-content;
    margin-top: 0.25rem;
  }

  /* Body */
  .story-body p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    /* ~80 characters a line (Nunito's "0" is wide, so 62ch ≈ 80 chars) */
    max-width: 62ch;
  }
  .story-body p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  /* Timeline — feature-colour dots with an ink ring on a faint rule */
  .story-timeline {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 2px dashed var(--ink-faint);
  }
  .timeline-heading {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .timeline {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }
  .timeline::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 6px;
    top: 4px;
    bottom: 4px;
    width: 2px;
    background: var(--ink-faint);
  }
  .timeline-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    position: relative;
  }
  .timeline-marker {
    position: absolute;
    left: -1.5rem;
    top: 4px;
    width: 14px;
    height: 14px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--color-leaf);
    border: 2px solid var(--color-ink);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px var(--bg-card);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .timeline-item:nth-child(3n + 2) .timeline-marker { background: var(--color-berry); }
  .timeline-item:nth-child(3n + 3) .timeline-marker { background: var(--color-sky); }
  .timeline-content {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.15rem;
  }
  .timeline-week {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
  .timeline-text {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  /* Quote — muted well with a red left rule */
  .story-quote {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    background: var(--bg-muted);
    border: 2px solid var(--ink-faint);
    border-left: 6px solid var(--color-accent);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }
  .story-quote p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
  }
  .story-quote cite {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  /* Booking button closing each story */
  .story-cta {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  /* CTA */
  .cta-section {
    background: var(--bg-secondary);
  }
  .cta-desc {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }
  /* The heading sat flush on the paragraph below it (0px gap) */
  .cta-section .section-heading {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  /* Tablet landscape and up: the story reads at a comfortable measure on the
     left while milestones + quote become a sidebar. As one full-width column
     the paragraphs ran 115–190 characters a line (1024px → 2560px) with the
     right half of every card's lower sections empty. */
  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .story-card {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 62ch) minmax(18rem, 1fr);
      grid-template-rows: auto auto auto 1fr;
      grid-template-areas:
        "head head"
        "body timeline"
        "body quote"
        "body cta";
      column-gap: 2.5rem;
    }
    .story-header { grid-area: head; }
    .story-body { grid-area: body; }
    .story-timeline {
      grid-area: timeline;
      margin-top: 0;
      padding-top: 0;
      border-top: 0;
    }
    .story-quote {
      grid-area: quote;
      align-self: start;
    }
    .story-cta {
      grid-area: cta;
      align-self: start;
    }
  }

  /* The global container widens to 1600–2200px here; a single column of
     stories stays at a readable width instead (rem, so it scales with the
     112.5–150% root size). */
  @media (min-width: 1441px) {
    .stories-section .container {
      max-width: 72rem;
    }
    /* rem, not px: at the 150% root the 720px cap minus 4rem padding left
       528px for 84px type, and "transformations" broke mid-word */
    .hero-content { max-width: 45rem; }
    .hero-subtitle { max-width: 31.25rem; }
  }
  /* the brand name never breaks at its hyphen ("A- / Worthy") */
  .nobr { white-space: nowrap; }

  /* Responsive */
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .story-card {
      padding: 1rem;
    }
    .story-header {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: 1rem;
    }
    .grade.chip {
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      padding: 0.3rem 0.8rem;
      min-height: 40px;
    }
    .story-name {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
    }
  }
</style>
